<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Phase 42.3 — real backup rules (this file replaced the Android Studio
    sample that shipped as-is since the project began; the sample had no
    <include>/<exclude>, so "back up essentially everything in app storage"
    was the effective policy — including the whole downloaded userland).

    Policy: an auto-backup carries ONLY what a person would call "my code".
    Everything a network re-download or a first run can rebuild stays out;
    anything device- or ABI-specific (the toolchain prefix) MUST stay out —
    a restore onto a different-ABI phone is otherwise an exec'ing-$PREFIX-
    shaped hole, and a GitHub token riding a cloud backup is exactly what
    GitRedactor exists to prevent elsewhere.

    The single include below is the whole backup scope: nothing outside it
    is ever copied. The excludes are belt-and-braces documents — they pin
    the dangerous paths so a future broadened <include> cannot silently drag
    the toolchain (or the token) into a backup. Host-pinned: BackupRulesTest.

    Deliberately NOT included:
      - files/datastore/settings.preferences_pb — the settings DataStore,
        which holds the GitHub token (GitCredentialsStore). A fresh install
        asks the user to sign in again; that is intentional, see
        docs/DATA_AND_PRIVACY.md.
      - files/usr, files/home — the downloaded userland/toolchain + dpkg
        state (hundreds of MB, ABI- and device-specific).
      - files/CodeC/{temp,modules,tcc} — regenerable run temp, downloaded
        compiler modules, and the extracted TCC bundle.
      - files/crash-log.txt — a crash record belongs to the build that
        wrote it, not to the next install.

    Products of these rules:
      CodeC/projects — the user's projects — ride auto-backup and
      device-to-device transfer, and nothing else does.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="file" path="CodeC/projects" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="usr" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="home" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="CodeC/temp" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="CodeC/modules" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="CodeC/tcc" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="crash-log.txt" />
</full-backup-content>
